074" :answer-field/id #uuid "896bf1f0-ba4b-535d-8282-a74335b3f33e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-36219/selection/ma-v1/30acb569ad7baaa7e9a8c74d7705411bb5474d5616daeb9daae5051bb7e0d074/bfe6285fa2a3c82f6fc303aadc50d6645a928fe5cb15c2829aa6d853b06d4dea" :answer-field/choices ["q-36219/selection/ma-v1/30acb569ad7baaa7e9a8c74d7705411bb5474d5616daeb9daae5051bb7e0d074/31cee71e6278382eeb04d97a3c3bd3d9b1eeef95ae22bb860e756b29265ea60d" "q-36219/selection/ma-v1/30acb569ad7baaa7e9a8c74d7705411bb5474d5616daeb9daae5051bb7e0d074/bfe6285fa2a3c82f6fc303aadc50d6645a928fe5cb15c2829aa6d853b06d4dea" "q-36219/selection/ma-v1/30acb569ad7baaa7e9a8c74d7705411bb5474d5616daeb9daae5051bb7e0d074/86b1b15ecdf3028aa495ba964a6783d0ac3ac8755a14a0f5000386f4ccc6c69a" "q-36219/selection/ma-v1/30acb569ad7baaa7e9a8c74d7705411bb5474d5616daeb9daae5051bb7e0d074/2ea527d03e0e9930722bd518f02ad8bfe0df8e6964c41675f3271d5173634883" "q-36219/selection/ma-v1/30acb569ad7baaa7e9a8c74d7705411bb5474d5616daeb9daae5051bb7e0d074/e5b4106f56de417ba7c4d2436054b291c39a347b1ead559fc4436d54571ca007"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-36219"] :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=1.$ Given that the point $P(1,2,4)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=\\frac{3x+y}{\\sqrt{6xy+{y}^{2}}}$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(1,2,4)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(1,2)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}$ at $(1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(1,2) & =\\frac{3(1)+(2)}{\\sqrt{6(1)(2)+(2)^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{\\sqrt{16}} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(1,2)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(1,2)}(y-2) \\\\ z-4 & =\\frac{5}{4}(y-2) \\\\ z & =\\frac{5}{4}y+\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(1,2,4)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1 \\\\ z=\\frac{5}{4}y+\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-36219/selection/ma-v1/30acb569ad7baaa7e9a8c74d7705411bb5474d5616daeb9daae5051bb7e0d074"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-132587/selection/54bb8fd00e32fdf8ef7091ca2abb46dc0a33938a659b8a6193356f46cceefa82" :answer/id #uuid "51b22bb7-db06-5bad-9384-34af6ed679e8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\\\ z=6x+3\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132587/selection/4e1e6e79ecd8e0671afcb80e590879b142b44706f6a607e7bed9dd13d05c911d" :answer/id #uuid "2e60d34e-02b2-5978-b117-a667cb9ca579" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\\\ z=3x-2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132587/selection/27eb509c5ed067e671e74562289d3563b880da927359f4225cda3698379152a2" :answer/id #uuid "5535b1d3-0529-5411-b513-6a8eeebc8b8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\\\ z=3x-5\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132587/selection/841bc80c4d496438d82dc3d70f05edc9f980e060e95faec8cdfce07f52af382f" :answer/id #uuid "c75587ad-2a40-5b14-91f0-e672131fad70" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\\\ z=4x+3\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132587/selection/6457b618be680da392f79ce424b933fc9c73aae9e05c4d2b2ea0dac6a9ca4142" :answer/id #uuid "62be1fc5-e9da-52c3-914b-0cf766b7145d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\\\ z=6x-5\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132587/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ae4e4c26-14dd-5edd-9ebd-badb52824707" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132587/selection/6457b618be680da392f79ce424b933fc9c73aae9e05c4d2b2ea0dac6a9ca4142" :answer-field/choices ["q-132587/selection/54bb8fd00e32fdf8ef7091ca2abb46dc0a33938a659b8a6193356f46cceefa82" "q-132587/selection/4e1e6e79ecd8e0671afcb80e590879b142b44706f6a607e7bed9dd13d05c911d" "q-132587/selection/27eb509c5ed067e671e74562289d3563b880da927359f4225cda3698379152a2" "q-132587/selection/841bc80c4d496438d82dc3d70f05edc9f980e060e95faec8cdfce07f52af382f" "q-132587/selection/6457b618be680da392f79ce424b933fc9c73aae9e05c4d2b2ea0dac6a9ca4142"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132587" :question/id #uuid "65b6a4c9-d497-51fc-b78a-818d9d90b8fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-132587" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $y=2.$ Given that the point $P(1,2,1)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}=2xy+2$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $y=2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(1,2,1)$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1,2)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂x}$ at $(1,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1,2)} & =2(1)(2)+2 \\\\  & =4+2 \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(1,2)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂x}{|}_{(1,2)}(x-1) \\\\ z-1 & =6(x-1) \\\\ z & =6x-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(1,2,1)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y=2 \\\\ z=6x-5\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-132587/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c5685f7-71b2-58ae-8c61-f555b355d92f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132587"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132595/selection/d9e44d866f9075688af15456b3e721f0f72404f3c980acff506a4430b8f05208" :answer/id #uuid "f5e4bec9-e9a6-5d37-acc4-6b6af9581f4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ z=-\\frac{1}{4}y-2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132595/selection/c669dc7c154c5aa4c59788962464c12126e34cfa29d8f419b19fecad001cbc62" :answer/id #uuid "9ad33dab-823c-5cbf-aae5-94ac4bbd9ed6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ z=\\frac{1}{2}y+2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132595/selection/587b0ba493a7c39b99d2e6f4c805f53c5c13fc9990232e227632419c55085dbc" :answer/id #uuid "f43633ae-9118-5fb5-8924-8d9d38ed6b6c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ z=-\\frac{3}{4}y+2\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132595/selection/aa6862614537a64b568dc264e6d0191a4e9dc76a7d1b6403f43f1b92bd663ea4" :answer/id #uuid "9a3342aa-db4c-58cc-810a-00e95c556260" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ z=\\frac{3}{2}y-1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132595/selection/83f911b453260de85f82108e91fea35c2b9225dcfd4218c1d42d8c38e0592ba0" :answer/id #uuid "dd66e5b1-b0d7-510d-902f-6af28619ad8c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}x=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ z=-\\frac{3}{2}y+1\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132595/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "42ac90ee-1bdb-505d-b1b9-a5d78e62d51e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132595/selection/587b0ba493a7c39b99d2e6f4c805f53c5c13fc9990232e227632419c55085dbc" :answer-field/choices ["q-132595/selection/d9e44d866f9075688af15456b3e721f0f72404f3c980acff506a4430b8f05208" "q-132595/selection/c669dc7c154c5aa4c59788962464c12126e34cfa29d8f419b19fecad001cbc62" "q-132595/selection/587b0ba493a7c39b99d2e6f4c805f53c5c13fc9990232e227632419c55085dbc" "q-132595/selection/aa6862614537a64b568dc264e6d0191a4e9dc76a7d1b6403f43f1b92bd663ea4" "q-132595/selection/83f911b453260de85f82108e91fea35c2b9225dcfd4218c1d42d8c38e0592ba0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132595" :question/id #uuid "90feb6cc-3983-5462-9881-e7dbb7d7a0f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-132595" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=\\sqrt{2}.$ Given that the point $P(\\sqrt{2},2,\\frac{1}{2})$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}=-\\frac{2{x}^{2}+y}{{y}^{3}}$, find the equations of the tangent line to $C$ at $P.$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface $z=f(x,y)$ with the plane $x=\\sqrt{2}.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve at the point $P(\\sqrt{2},2,\\frac{1}{2})$ will be given by the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(\\sqrt{2},2)}.$\n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative $\\frac{∂z}{∂y}$ at $(\\sqrt{2},2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(\\sqrt{2},2) & =-\\frac{2(\\sqrt{2})^{2}+2}{{2}^{3}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{4+2}{8} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-z{|}_{(\\sqrt{2},2)} & =\\frac{∂z}{∂y}{|}_{(\\sqrt{2},2)}(y-2) \\\\ z-\\frac{1}{2} & =-\\frac{3}{4}(y-2) \\\\ z & =-\\frac{3}{4}y+2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(\\sqrt{2},2,\\frac{1}{2})$ can be given as the intersection of two planes, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=\\sqrt{2} \\\\ z=-\\frac{3}{4}y+2\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-132595/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4c5685f7-71b2-58ae-8c61-f555b355d92f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132595"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132601/selection/69d128fb780b53f5c6cf304fe0b33828659ad94835e94b7dfd8e0a5f36c4402e" :answer/id #uuid "ca3ce60a-93d2-53e6-8882-c89d623a9e10" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "j+2\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132601/selection/902a12843964636c823ef343139da85213975a4082235450d84284954b72a566" :answer/id #uuid "fcd669da-ce2e-57b5-af70-442799426116" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3\\,j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132601/selection/dc2ac4782fe795c9aeab3257828751bc602a58880fd56416a3930e35749b5d6c" :answer/id #uuid "1e2ced03-0d0e-5009-83cc-26a21ff53991" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\,j+3\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132601/selection/5e5361b552a39f6dd85fed8609de801e754fca23406835015d297ddd25e664e4" :answer/id #uuid "cfd92310-90b2-582f-84db-234cd0ca623c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "j-3\\,k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132601/selection/7dd27701a1d3aa50ba174c2d35e6ca5e3f7b406c3065eb75d249d79365dd97bf" :answer/id #uuid "770e6717-4d6d-56b4-b15d-1143ab390c4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2\\,j+k" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132601/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "38009d16-d2ad-5654-ae55-e75bed727df8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132601/selection/69d128fb780b53f5c6cf304fe0b33828659ad94835e94b7dfd8e0a5f36c4402e" :answer-field/choices ["q-132601/selection/69d128fb780b53f5c6cf304fe0b33828659ad94835e94b7dfd8e0a5f36c4402e" "q-132601/selection/902a12843964636c823ef343139da85213975a4082235450d84284954b72a566" "q-132601/selection/dc2ac4782fe795c9aeab3257828751bc602a58880fd56416a3930e35749b5d6c" "q-132601/selection/5e5361b552a39f6dd85fed8609de801e754fca23406835015d297ddd25e664e4" "q-132601/selection/7dd27701a1d3aa50ba174c2d35e6ca5e3f7b406c3065eb75d249d79365dd97bf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132601" :question/id #uuid "3e93bbd2-d64e-547a-8b0e-91b9a4e6aa38" :question/math-academy-id "q-132601" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $x=-2.$ Given that the point $P(-2,2,3)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{y}={x}^{2}y+2x-y$, which of the following gives a tangent vector to $C$ at $P?$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface with the plane $x=-2.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(-2,2).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{y}(x,y)$ at $(-2,2):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{y}(-2,2) & =(-2)^{2}(2)+2(-2)-(2) \\\\  & =8-4-2 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(-2,2) & ={f}_{y}(-2,2)(y-2) \\\\ z-3 & =2(y-2) \\\\ z & =2y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(-2,2,3)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-2 \\\\ z=2y-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $x=-2,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨1,0,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=2y-1$ (or $2y-z-1=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨0,2,-1⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨1,0,0⟩\\times ⟨0,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =j+2\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, a tangent vector to $C$ at $P$ is $j+2\\,k.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-132601/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0325887-ce25-5d6f-bf27-d85541e1dbe0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132601"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-132602/selection/eee5a3a8e12930dd100249b1242ad7e1794b48a6f0e204e718f698c7792ed534" :answer/id #uuid "1d94c907-2e6e-55f1-8424-a786cc1724e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,0,-1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132602/selection/eb908f0e417b7f384ee1a38bcb321a91d362f85adf19a7a7bc1500a3dd860f28" :answer/id #uuid "6e2e5ac1-ca46-526f-afed-e1507f7a295c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨-1,0,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132602/selection/1bcb2fdfe136c211d7aaed44fb976bb11f8aa790f5ceb5878f3f6a915632de3d" :answer/id #uuid "ead71636-829d-5b75-b1c0-ecd981622383" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,0,2⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132602/selection/eca61f1b84786d16ad626af7ba601bb554c91c7a8e27048a60a489599617710e" :answer/id #uuid "58f6f420-e3f7-5eda-ac45-92e3f2d2934c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨1,0,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132602/selection/e06fdd0a26fec13f39b4f355b73b63c43979b6aeafe4528e93509bca1a5a2b37" :answer/id #uuid "9dea61ef-3d3f-5c8a-a8d2-ed073c9afab9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "⟨2,0,1⟩" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-132602/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "546c7e1b-42aa-5583-a579-3cc21ab4220e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-132602/selection/eca61f1b84786d16ad626af7ba601bb554c91c7a8e27048a60a489599617710e" :answer-field/choices ["q-132602/selection/eee5a3a8e12930dd100249b1242ad7e1794b48a6f0e204e718f698c7792ed534" "q-132602/selection/eb908f0e417b7f384ee1a38bcb321a91d362f85adf19a7a7bc1500a3dd860f28" "q-132602/selection/1bcb2fdfe136c211d7aaed44fb976bb11f8aa790f5ceb5878f3f6a915632de3d" "q-132602/selection/eca61f1b84786d16ad626af7ba601bb554c91c7a8e27048a60a489599617710e" "q-132602/selection/e06fdd0a26fec13f39b4f355b73b63c43979b6aeafe4528e93509bca1a5a2b37"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-132602" :question/id #uuid "e7a0ef21-1ab3-5b2b-a1e5-8efa25c0c00b" :question/math-academy-id "q-132602" :question/problem "The curve $C$ is the intersection of a surface $S,$ defined by $z=f(x,y),$ with the plane $y=1.$ Given that the point $P(0,1,7)$ lies on $C$, and that ${f}_{x}={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+y)$, which of the following gives a tangent vector to $C$ at $P?$" :question/worked-solution "The curve $C$ is the intersection of the surface with the plane $y=1.$ Hence, the slope of the tangent to the curve $C$ at the point $P$ will be given by the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(0,1).$ \n\nTo get the slope, we evaluate the partial derivative ${f}_{x}(x,y)$ at $(0,1):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(0,1) & ={0}^{2}+{1}^{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(0+1) \\\\  & =0+1-0 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we use the point-slope form of a straight line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z-f(0,1) & ={f}_{x}(0,1)(x-0) \\\\ z-7 & =1(x) \\\\ z & =x+7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the tangent line to the curve $C$ at $P(0,1,7)$ can be given as the intersection of two planes:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}y=1 \\\\ z=x+7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $y=1,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨0,1,0⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $z=x+7$ (or $x-z+7=0$), a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,0,-1⟩.$\n\nFinally, to find a direction vector for the tangent line, we calculate the cross product of these normal vectors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨0,1,0⟩\\times ⟨1,0,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =-i-\\,k \\\\  & =⟨-1,0,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $⟨-1,0,-1⟩$ is parallel to the tangent line, then $-⟨-1,0,-1⟩=⟨1,0,1⟩$ is also parallel to it." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-132602/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0325887-ce25-5d6f-bf27-d85541e1dbe0"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-132602"] :db/ensure [